 "explain": [
  "hero run 15 (Nov 2 2026), pod hero7d, one RTX PRO 6000, the expert GEMM form (dev/hero/bench_grouped.py): synthetic banks of the released model's shapes (K 5120, I 2304, top-6), the pairs' experts drawn at random over 192 slots (384 at 990 pairs) so a call's distinct count matches a real step's (39 at 48 pairs, 89 at 240, 191 at 990), alternating slot halves so the 128 MB L2 never serves a repeat, 8 to 10 calls a point under the CUDA profiler; bytes counted per distinct expert at the 1,535 GB/s read peak.",
  "the grouped kernels before this run (plain loads, gate and up in one program, BM 16, BN 64, BK 128): 48 pairs 558 us (87% of the floor), 240 pairs 1,780 (61%), 990 over 192 slots 2,076 (57%).",
  "the GEMM form, 48 tile sets (BM 16/32, BN 32/64, BK 128/256, warps 2/4, stages 2/3/4), gate/up and down with the same set: best (16, 32, 128, 2 warps, 3 stages) at 48 pairs 532 us (90%), 240 pairs 1,183 (93%), 990 pairs 2,526 (93%); (16, 64, 128, 4, 3) within 1%; BK 256 costs 8% (1,279 at 240 pairs); BM 32 is a loss everywhere (half-empty blocks at these pair counts: 2,404 at 48 pairs), so the block stays 16 pairs.",
  "bit-identical to the grouped kernels at every pair count (the same dots in the same order; the tile shape changes only the tensor core's grouping, not the fp32 sums' order within a block)."
 ],
